// Bitcoin Script Macro Examples
// Demonstrates wallet-side macro expansion to base opcodes

// Example 1: hashCat - duplicates, hashes, and concatenates
// Expands to: dup sha256 swap cat
// Result: [x || SHA256(x)]
"hello" hashCat

// Stack now contains: ["hello", "<hash of hello>hello"]

// Example 2: xSwap_n - swap top with nth item
// Set up a stack with multiple values
drop drop  // Clear previous
1 2 3 4 5

// xSwap_2 swaps top (5) with 2nd from top (3)
// Stack: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] -> [1, 2, 5, 4, 3]
xSwap_2

// Example 3: xDrop_n - drop nth item from stack
// Stack: [1, 2, 5, 4, 3]
// xDrop_2 drops 2nd from top (4)
// Stack: [1, 2, 5, 3]
xDrop_2

// Example 4: xRot_n - rotate nth item to top
// Stack: [1, 2, 5, 3]
// xRot_3 brings 3rd from top (2) to the top
// Stack: [1, 5, 3, 2]
xRot_3

// Example 5: LOOP[n]{body} - unroll a loop n times
// This pushes 0, 1, 2 onto the stack
LOOP[3]{$i}

// Stack now has: [1, 5, 3, 2, 0, 1, 2]

// LOOP with operations
drop drop drop drop drop drop drop  // Clear stack

// Push 5 copies of 100
LOOP[5]{100}

// Stack: [100, 100, 100, 100, 100]
// Sum them all: 100 + 100 + 100 + 100 + 100 = 500
add add add add

// Final stack should contain: [500]
